{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1482729-awakend-mages-in-abyssless-settings","id":1482729,"title":"Awakend mages in abyssless settings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-06-02T02:29:41-07:00","id":1482729,"title":"Awakend mages in abyssless settings","content":"Ive been thinking about crossovers lately and ive been wondering how one might handle an awakened mage who found themselves in another universe, and how (on a simple level) that might effect their mechanics.<br /> <br /> Even the settings with abyssal equivalents don't tend too have them blocking off the supernal(if an equivalent can be found)<br /> <br /> I am curious as too how people would approach this, and what you would have as a penalty for overreaching, as treating most settings as demesnes seems too much.<br /> <br /> My own approach would be too have the possibility of reality warping in non abyssal manners, magic can go awry even if it would be maliciously corrupting. I would also probably have mages be pathless, as they don't need the watchtowers too cross the abyss, a bit like how i think arc mages work if remember right. depending on the setting an extra point of reach might be resonable as well.<br /> <br /> The setting that brought on this thought process is actually DC, and like the source wall is within that universe, if a bit of a physical distance. I could see DC being a setting too give a free reach (perhaps even two tbh) but also DC likes too doom its magic users. You could have a build up of some kind of not easily removable curse on you should generate paradox that can screw you over in some thematic way tied too that characters Doom. might be removable if you use that fate spell that creates a path too fixing something but at least then it forces a quest on you.<br /> <br /> I would love too see what other people might have as ideas on how they would handle it<br /> <br /> Also what setting would you drop a mage, of any skill level, too see the most interesting story emerge?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6947-cubleds","name":"cubleds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T06:59:36-07:00","id":1482741,"title":"","content":"Mechanics-wise, not much would be changed. Most of Paradox/Dissonance is already \u201cyou screwed up your spell, which in turns screws you and anyone around you\u201d stuff. The Abyss is not needed to explain them. You\u2019ll have to explain away Abyssal Entities though; most likely as powerful Ephemeral Entities who have a vested interest in teaching some manners to uppity mages for some ancient reason.<br /> <br /> Lore-wise, most of the Orders would have to be completely reworked. I wouldn\u2019t go too deep into them ATM\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh, speaking more of Paradox; have you checked out Ars Magica and Mage The Ascension? The former has Warpings, as \u2018natural\u2019 consequences of overexposure to supernatural powers. The latter has Paradox too, caused by friction with the Consensus, but most of them manifest as \u2018logical\u2019 consequences of your specific Mystical/ Hyperscientific practices, so you can forage that for ideas too. In fact, there was a thread in that game\u2019s subforum on this site about exactly that, called 1001 Paradoxes or something (forgot the exact name). Try searching it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T08:28:44-07:00","id":1482767,"title":"","content":"Another thing to consider is that without the Abyss, there is no Lie nor Quiescence. That is, mortal observers don't cause magic to unravel; mortals don't lose their memories of Supernal phenomena; and mortals aren't subject to Integrity loss from exposure to Supernal phenomena. In effect, the world is populated entirely by Sleepwalkers and Awakened; there are no Sleepers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T09:33:42-07:00","id":1482777,"title":"","content":"^clarifying a note on that, Sleepwalkers would be the dominant form of humanity, not mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 06-02-2022, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T12:16:53-07:00","id":1482811,"title":"","content":"Considering how useful and flexible magic is, I would imagine being Awakened in such a setting would be very unpleasant. Mages can get incredibly helpful information remarkably fast, they can pull clues out of thin air using Focused Mage Sight. They can craft items of incredible quality, survive in otherwise impossible situations just using magic, even work more quickly and efficiently than anyone else. When combined with the fact that any high skill mage can no sell anything mundane via Shielding (no Disbelief means their defenses are a lot more durable) and that they have an innate access to the collective unconscious (one of the few supernaturals who have an all access pass) means they would be seen as supersoldiers. So governments, secret societies and the like would probably want to seize, brainwash or create some dependency (think Ketracel-white from Star Trek), since whoever controls the supernatural power has a major edge in whatever field they are focused on.<br /> <br /> Regarding which setting I would use, probably <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/TabletopGame/UnknownArmies\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Unknown Armies</i></a>. Since the more magic you have in that setting, the more insane you are. Sleepwalkers and ritual casters tend to have the highest positions in secrets societies and conspiracies, because the Adepts (the name for the different type of mages) are not functional enough to handle it. Adepts derive their powers via believing in logical paradoxes to the point the world simply rolls with it. The fact the Awakened don't would be unusual, especially since they do not need to be insane to function or need to procure insanely rare or specific components for any major casting. You have the Invisible College as an end goal similar to Ascension. Putting it all together would drop the Awakened in a very unique position to overturn the status quo, profit handsomely and gain quite a few Arcane Beats along the way, if they are smart about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 06-02-2022, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T00:59:29-07:00","id":1482906,"title":"","content":"I am running a setting like this (inspired by the Johnathan Strange and Mister Norrel novel), the Abyss is definitely still a thing, but there is no lie. <br /> <br /> Mechanically, no Quiessence or Dissonance, overreaching still causes paradox/wild magic. <br /> <br /> I have entirely removed the orders (there are no Exarchs, so no Seers). But kept the paths, because it is less effort for my world building.<br /> <br /> In the aftermath of Johnathan Strange helping win the Napoleonic wars, every European power now wants their own mages, so the players have found themselves in a magical arms race.<br /> <br /> Proto-orders are forming, left-handed mages backed by Imperial powers are sneaking around with little/no checks and balanced, and some factions want to create as masquerade to avoid political institutions interfering with their Obsessions...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 06-03-2022, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T01:28:18-07:00","id":1482908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1482729-awakend-mages-in-abyssless-settings?p=1482811#post1482811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> they would be seen as supersoldiers. So governments, secret societies and the like would probably want to seize, brainwash or create some dependency (think Ketracel-white from Star Trek), since whoever controls the supernatural power has a major edge in whatever field they are focused on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Mwahaha, I see you as a supersoldier!&quot;<br /> {Two-dot Mind spell}<br /> &quot;I see you as a kitty. Who's a pretty kitty?&quot;<br /> <br /> I feel as though your case for mage strength weakens your case for mage vulnerability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T12:30:56-07:00","id":1482959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cubleds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1482729-awakend-mages-in-abyssless-settings#post1482729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> I would love too see what other people might have as ideas on how they would handle it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I'd leave the Abyss right where it is. Most settings are unaffected by such a hidden facet of reality.<br /> <br /> It's actually more work if the setting <i>has</i> an Abyss equivalent realm but with differences than if it simply lacks one. You've only got to explain why it hasn't come up and you're done, as opposed to rectifying any discrepancies without creating new ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}